      en: "Sowa (formerly Sowa Pan) is a town in Botswana's Central District, on the eastern edge of the Makgadikgadi salt pans. It was founded in the 1990s as a mining town for the soda ash (sodium carbonate) mine. The town hosts the soda ash production operated by Botash, a joint venture between the Botswana government and two multinational companies. Sowa has modern infrastructure with housing, schools, and a hospital. Population is about 3,000. Extreme temperatures and remote location define life. The salt pans attract tourists, especially for flamingos and other birds.",
